the Sony Walkman zx2 isn't like any  Walkman you've seen before it plays high  resolution audio files and will set you  back a whopping 1200 dollars this isn't  one for the casual listener zx2 itself  is really well made the metal body is a  textured leather back and a gold audio  jack not so subtly telling you that the  components inside are top of the line it  feels like a serious piece of audio  equipment but it's heavier and bulkier  than I'd like for daily use inside is a  128 gigabyte hard drive that you'll have  to expand pretty quickly with a microSD  card to hold those larger high  definition audio files the interface is  Android base but feels laggy at times  and while the physical buttons on the  side or a good idea practically they're  hard to get used to after years of only  using touch screens the real question  though is how the ZX two sounds  listening with a pair of quality  headphones on my couch or at my desk  music sounded incredible it was rich it  was textured and I loved it but the  moment I stepped out into the real world  any noticeable difference disappeared  there are just too many distractions and  too much ambient noise I love the idea  of a high-end gadget that does one thing  really well but considering the limited  audio benefits the burden of carrying  another heavy device and the steep price  I'm giving the ZX to a pass by a good  pair of headphones instead save that  extra cash for the next Taylor Swift  album
 

